Subject: Fail a ColorBuffer asked for while the device is lost, instead of ending the stream

A GPU reset loses the renderer's Vulkan device, and 0021 makes it again on a thread of its own
while the guest's calls that need it fail at once. A ColorBuffer asked for in that time cannot
be made, and FrameBuffer took that for a fatal error: it aborted, which (with aemu's 0002)
ended the guest's stream. The guest process lost its renderer connection over a call that
works again a few milliseconds later. When the ColorBuffer could not be made because the
device was lost (it is not usable now, or a loss was counted during the call), the call
fails instead: rcCreateColorBuffer answers handle 0, and a ColorBuffer asked for under the
guest's own handle is not made, which the guest's next open finds. The stream stays, and the
same call makes the ColorBuffer on the new device. Any other failure stays fatal.

Applies after 0028 on gfxstream d047a57228332d995d36600792fa9ccc26cf8ae6.
---
diff --git a/host/FrameBuffer.cpp b/host/FrameBuffer.cpp
--- a/host/FrameBuffer.cpp
+++ b/host/FrameBuffer.cpp
@@ -1201,9 +1201,22 @@ HandleType FrameBuffer::createColorBufferWithResourceHandleLocked(int p_width, int p_height,
                                                                   GLenum p_internalFormat,
                                                                   FrameworkFormat p_frameworkFormat,
                                                                   HandleType handle) {
+    // A GPU reset loses the Vulkan device, and a ColorBuffer asked for until the device is
+    // made again cannot be made. That is not the guest's fault and not fatal: the call fails
+    // (handle 0, or no ColorBuffer under the guest's handle, which the guest's next open
+    // finds), the guest's stream stays, and the same call works on the new device.
+    const uint64_t lossesBefore = m_emulationVk ? m_emulationVk->deviceLosses() : 0;
     ColorBufferPtr cb =
         ColorBuffer::create(m_emulationGl.get(), m_emulationVk.get(), p_width, p_height,
                             p_internalFormat, p_frameworkFormat, handle, nullptr /*stream*/);
+    if (cb.get() == nullptr && m_emulationVk &&
+        (!m_emulationVk->deviceUsable() || m_emulationVk->deviceLosses() != lossesBefore)) {
+        ERR("Could not make ColorBuffer %u (%dx%d, format 0x%x): the renderer's Vulkan device "
+            "was lost and is being made again. The guest's call fails; it works again once "
+            "the new device is made.",
+            handle, p_width, p_height, p_internalFormat);
+        return 0;
+    }
     if (cb.get() == nullptr) {
         GFXSTREAM_ABORT(FatalError(ABORT_REASON_OTHER))
             << "Failed to create ColorBuffer:" << handle << " format:" << p_internalFormat
